* Microchip MCP41010 - 10 kohm, 8-bit (256 position) digital potentiometer
*
* Pins: A W B   (PA0 / PW0 / PB0)
* D   = wiper code 0..255 (power-on value 128)
* RAB = end-to-end resistance (10 k nominal, ±20 % part to part)
* RW  = wiper switch resistance (52 ohm typ, 100 ohm max)
*
*   R_WB = RAB * D / 256         R_AW = RAB * (256 - D) / 256
*
* Static model only: the SPI interface is replaced by the D parameter.
* The terminal capacitances are approximate. Check the datasheet
* (CA/CB/CW) if you care about behaviour above ~100 kHz.

.subckt MCP41010 A W B D=128 RAB=10k RW=52
Raw A wi {max(RAB*(256-D)/256, 1m)}
Rwb wi B {max(RAB*D/256, 1m)}
Rwip wi W {RW}
Ca A 0 10p
Cb B 0 10p
Cw W 0 5.6p
.ends MCP41010
